###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# All training runs used one NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3090 (24 GiB). The
# augmentations add no backward passes or memory to training (Table 7);
# no times are given.

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - ts1x-val and RGD1 errors are given in the text (Figs. 7 and 8 plot them); where the text gives only a range over UniAug and ModeAug (EquiformerV2 direct force: ts1x-val energy 0.0227-0.0280 eV and force 0.0099-0.0111 eV/A; RGD1 force 0.1017-0.1044 eV/A and ModeAug energy 0.8586-0.9509 eV) no value is encoded. Energy MAEs are per structure in eV.
# - The 1:3 augmentation-ratio and sigma = 0.10 A ModeAug variants are mentioned with single values (0.1017 and 0.1041 eV/A out of domain) but are not encoded as separate models. HessianQM9 validation force MAEs (Table 2) are not encoded because the architecture is not named for that study.
# - Hessian, eigenvalue, asymmetry and n_imag errors (Tables 5, 6), MD17 force cosines (Table 3) and MD stability and h(r) errors (Table 4) have no metric property in the schema. GotenNet is a new registry method (its method paper is not in the corpus).
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: datacite).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/kwak2026.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.

